#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Iowa
#> pause: 40
#> must: Alabama
#> must: Iowa
#> must: # command:  sed  -f
#> not: Kansas
#> not: Montana
#> source: N;$!P;$!D;$d
# 24. Delete the last two lines. Pement: sed 'N;$!P;$!D;$d'
# The same two-line window as tail -2 (step 16), run the other way round:
# P prints the first line of the window and D slides it down, until the
# window reaches the last line, where $d throws both lines away. sed '$d'
# alone deletes just the last line; sed '1,10d' deletes the first ten.
# Try: GNU's  0~2d  deletes every second line instead.
N;$!P;$!D;$d

#DATA
Alabama
Alaska
Iowa
Kansas
Montana
